A||||4||Child Of Rod||Picked up my Fieros,  where should I start?(LONG)||||1||
Z||000000||Child Of Rod||04-30-2000||03:42 AM||||I finally got my fieros towed.  Cost me $150 bucks to tow both of them. I opened them up cleaned out the pines needles, and leaves.<BR>Now I just need to know where to start.<BR>I am not very experienced with mechanical stuff, I mostly do body work.<BR>I can do an oil change, and a tune-up.<BR>I have pulled Small blocks from classis mustangs before, I just don't know where to start on pulling the engines.<BR>I would like to put a v8 kit in one of theses, as I know I can have a 350 v8 for about 300 bucks, but maybe a 3800 swap would be better?<BR>How much does a 3800 swap cost?(the kit form, plus the engine)?<BR>Is it easy to install?<BR>I also need to rebuild one of the 4- cylinder engines, so I have it extra, just in case I find I want 2 fieros.<BR>I know I may be unintelligible(it's 3:40 am here in NY) but please someone help me!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||04-30-2000||07:39 AM||||V8 or 3800 swaps aren't cheap figure at least $5k+ by the time you get everything finished. Easy job? NO If you have even the slightest question about your abilities have it done by someone who has done one before. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||04-30-2000||08:20 AM||||Just a suggestion, start out with something relatively easy that you know you can handle. This will sort of get your feet wet in a non-threatening manner. Then move to the bigger problems later. How about the electrical system, does everything work when you put a battery in? Check brakes, steering parts, ans suspension for worn out parts. Good luck! Remember, we'll be here for assistance and moral support. I'm glad to hear a couple more Fieros will be returning to the street in the future. P.S. Phil is right about the engine swaps, not for the faint of heart.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-30-2000||10:00 AM||||Or the weak of wallet!||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||04-30-2000||07:35 PM||||3800 's are great especially the SC engines. I have one in my 88 and I love it !!!Have had no problems. But You will pay for it. I got a steal of a deal on the engine but I still ended paying $5,500 easy. It costs money but man ! what an engine. it was made for this car. ||||reg||1
